{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":29,"result":{"isIncomplete":false,"items":[{"label":"id","kind":3,"detail":"fn id() -> u32","documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"The identifier the system gave this program."}},{"label":"ExitStatus","kind":22,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"How a program ended."}},{"label":"Output","kind":22,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"What a program printed and how it ended."}},{"label":"Stdio","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"What a stream of a started program is, as Rust's `Stdio`."}},{"label":"ChildStdin","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"The stdin of a started program, a pipe this program writes, as Rust's `ChildStdin`. Its `drop`\ncloses it, so that the program sees the end of its input."}},{"label":"ChildStdout","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"The stdout of a started program, a pipe this program reads, as Rust's `ChildStdout`, closed by\nits `drop`."}},{"label":"ChildStderr","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"The stderr of a started program, as `ChildStdout` is its stdout."}},{"label":"Child","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"A program started by `Command::spawn`, which runs while this one goes on, as Rust's `Child`. Its piped streams are `Some` until taken: `child.stdin.take()`."}},{"label":"Command","kind":7,"documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"A program to run, with its arguments, environment, directory and streams. Each method returns\nthe command itself, so calls chain: `new Command(\"git\").arg(\"status\").output()`."}},{"label":"exit","kind":3,"detail":"fn exit(code: i32) -> never","documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"Ends the program with the exit code `code`."}},{"label":"abort","kind":3,"detail":"fn abort() -> never","documentation":{"kind":"markdown","value":"Ends the program at once, abnormally."}}]}}
